1. Create a repository:
git init

2. Create a file:
echo Hello GitHub > hello.txt

3. Check the files:
dir

4. Add the file:
git add hello.txt

5. Commit the file:
git commit -m "First commit"

6. Rename the branch:
git branch -M main

7. Connect GitHub repository:
git remote add origin https://github.com/sivapriyakumar246-cyber/GitExperiment1.git

8. Upload to GitHub:
git push -u origin main

9. Check repository status:
git status

10. View commit history:
git log --oneline
